


   =====( TrionText V1.00 )=============================================


        Trion 'TrionText' Door.

        (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '96-'97. All rights reserved.

        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================

      TrionText is a sort of 'teletext' or 'ceefax' styled door.
      It tries to simulate Teletext to create some sort of
      bulletin system.


      You can start it with:


      Cmd "A" , 0-255
         CliDoor  "doors:TrionText/TrionText ~50"
      EndCmd


      Or if you want to use an other config as the default:


      Cmd "A" , 0-255
         CliDoor  "doors:TrionText/TrionText ~50 Config"
      EndCmd


      The default configuration file is:  "doors:TrionText/TrionText.cfg"
      And if your config is in the "doors:TrionText/Pages/" directory
      you don't have to specify the path.

      In the config file is the path where the text pages are
      and the number of seconds between cycling of (sub)pages.
      Default pages path is: "doors:TrionText/Pages/"


      At the start of the programm the directory with
      pages is scanned so the programm knows which
      screens exists .. with speeds up walking
      through screens.


      Pages are just plain ANSI files with no screen clearing codes.

      You have to use the folowing naming of the pages:

      normal pages are called (for pages 0 through 999):

      "Page.000.1"   Through   "Page.999.1"

      Note that the first page loaded will always be "Page.100.1"

      Every screen can have subpages by substituting the .1 number
      by continues numbering up to .999
      Note that there are no leading zero's in the subpage number,
      and that the page number always consist of 3 digits.

      Note that you can only goto Pages and that Subpages
      are cycled through automatically when you are on a
      page with subpages.
      Subpages are best used for animation, in this case
      they will have the same text but the graphics will
      be slighty different.
        


      Also there is a posiblity to make 'hidden' pages.
      These pages are shown after the R key is pressed.

      For this option you have to have a normal page
      like "Page.100.1" and a hiden page with an .R extension
      like "Page.100.1.R".
      Note that only the first SubPage can have an .R extension.




      The door is a little intelligent, at start it scans all
      pages so it doesn't trie to shown non-existing screens
      and it knows which are the previous and the next screens
      without any disk access.

      You can 'walk' through the pages with the +,- and return
      key, a little difference with the normal teletext system is
      that + or return leads to the next EXISTING page instead
      of just increasing the page counter with one.
      When you are at the last page, a return or + will lead
      to the first page in the system.
      The - key works in the same way but in the opposite direction.


      Also there is an editable helpscreen with the folowing
      keys:



          nnn          =   Goto page nnn
          space        =   Goto page 100
          +, return    =   Goto next page
          -            =   Goto previous page
          R            =   Reveal hidden data
          ?            =   Show helpscreen
          Q, esc       =   Quit programm


